verdict.prompt:
This is a phone photograph of one page from an archive, taken so that the page can be transcribed by OCR. Judge only the photograph's capture quality, not the document's own condition: faded ink, stains, creases, handwriting or a carbon copy belong to the document, not the capture.

Reply with one JSON object and nothing else:
{"quality": an integer 1-5 (5: every word as readable as on a flatbed scan; 3: most words readable with effort; 1: most words cannot be read), "retake": true if a second photograph would let noticeably more words be read, else false, "defects": a list of zero or more of ["motion_blur", "out_of_focus", "glare", "shadow", "uneven_lighting", "dark_or_noisy", "tilted", "compression_artifacts", "cut_off"], "worst": the one listed defect that costs the most words, or "none"}
